@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+# Refresh expired access tokens automatically (#64)
+
+Our partner integrations authenticate with short-lived OAuth access tokens
+(15 minutes) instead of static API keys. Today every caller has to catch the
+401, fetch a new token and rebuild the client.
+
+## What changes
+
+- New optional `refreshToken: () => Promise<AccessToken>` client option. When
+  it is set, `apiKey` is treated as the initial access token and
+  `apiKeyExpiresAt` (epoch ms) as its expiry.
+- Before each request the client refreshes the token if it expires within the
+  next 30 seconds (clock-skew margin).
+- If the API still answers `401`, the client refreshes once and re-sends the
+  request. A second `401` surfaces as `ApiError(401, "unauthorized")`. The
+  re-send does not consume one of the caller's `maxRetries`.
+- Concurrent requests share a single refresh, so a rotating refresh token is
+  only spent once.
+- Static API keys (no `refreshToken`) behave exactly as before.
+
+## Testing
+
+New `tests/client-auth.test.ts` covers refresh on 401, proactive refresh,
+giving up after a second 401, retry accounting and concurrent 401s.
